{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128239-rural-freeholds","id":128239,"title":"Rural freeholds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T07:55:57-07:00","id":128239,"title":"Rural freeholds","content":"My current group has requested a freehold based on our local area for our next game. The only problem is, we're in the middle of nowhere, scattered across four hamlets and a village on the Cumbrian coast not far from the Scottish border. Does anyone have any ideas of how to design a freehold in this sort of setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T08:18:58-07:00","id":128261,"title":"","content":"I think it would be an awesome idea. <br /> <br /> I can quite clearly envision a tight-knit freehold which took up a farm (an maybe some nice ancient rural custom, as sacrificing oxes or whatever to assure a good crop) and lives together in the same farm - house. Some of them may decide to live directly in the forest, or in some more far-away little house in the woods. <br /> <br /> - The changelings of the freehold come from a quite vast area: there should be at least a couple of freehold members (winter and spring, i would say) which scout around newspapers and strange events in order to save and recruit just escaped changeling.<br /> <br /> - The freehold is isolated: probably, there will be a huge amount of internal politic and bickering amongst the changeling.<br /> <br /> And what happens when a spring member decides to bring a van full of human tourist in order to bring &quot;fresh air&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> - The freehold may be is &quot;a little bit too strange&quot;: there may be reporter which are trying to have a scoop on &quot;Genetically modified organism&quot; (goblin fruits?) which are grown in the land, or industrial spies which would greatly pay in order to have the &quot;secret tecnologies&quot; which the freehold don't has. On the other hand, neighboring farmers may be not so happy to have such &quot;bizarre&quot; neighbors.<br /> <br /> <br /> - There is a lot of unexplored real world terrain nearby. Make it memorable. And, of course, you should put there at least some trod. And children. And wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T09:28:53-07:00","id":128307,"title":"","content":"My longest running game took place in an rural freehold located in the farmlands of Upstate New York. The freehold's area of influence covered the expanse of an entire county, with a population that numbered around 25. Most changelings lived relatively off the grid, off in abandoned farms in the hills, old factories and in small camps out in the woods. Hobgoblins played a bigger role in the freehold and the main antagonists was a collective of fetches and loyalists that called themselves &quot;The Grange.&quot;<br /> <br /> You have to remember that rural locales don't have the luxury of anonymity that more urban areas provide. There are fewer people, and as such, the citizenry will take note of strangers and their odd behaviors. A secret society of magical misfits would undoubtedly get the attention of superstitious country folk, especially in the World of Darkness, where the darkness and paranoia of the places outside of cities creates an almost palpable aura of fear. <br /> <br /> Also consider: The old ways and superstitions of the Old World may still exist out in East Bumblefuck, Wherever. I can see motleys of changelings becoming the little gods and the &quot;good folk&quot; of folklore in these places, taking guardianship of entire towns and reinforcing the old rituals. Still, this sort of setup still requires the changelings to remain hidden ... faith and magical thinking has a hard time existing in the presence of proof and taking up the traditional roles of ancient fairies can't be very good for one's Clarity.<br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is how the Hedge interacts with these less &quot;civilized&quot; places. In Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell, the English countryside is dotted with mysterious fairy roads and old goblin manors whose denizens occasionally abscond with well mannered Englishmen. Perhaps, the &quot;country&quot; has more active gates into the Hedge, and thus more fairy activity in its wild places. The relative safety of the city is absent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:48:32-07:00","id":128420,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember with Changeling is the size of the freehold can depend on the Trods and Gentry activity. A small town that sees more Gentry activity and/or has a number of trods making it more accessible from Arcadia can have as many or more Lost than a much larger area. Of course, if you want to stress how small it is that need not be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T12:01:54-07:00","id":128431,"title":"","content":"One possibility is that the Freehold is entirely within the Hedge; but to protect against the dangers of the Hedge, particularly everyone going crazy, they have anchored their Hollow with lots of pledges to the locals.<br /> <br /> Pledges = plot hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:13:14-07:00","id":129288,"title":"","content":"We're actually in an old coal-mining area over here, though the mines themselves are abandoned now. I was thinking that maybe we could repurpose the mines as the Commons? No-one goes down there if they can help it, so it wouldn't be hard for the changelings to re-fit the place, get the old tunnels shored up et cetera, if they got all the Wizened on the job. And can we please lay off on the 'superstitious simple country folk' stereotype? Alarmingly enough, the twenty-first century did not magically skip over everyone outside the cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T16:00:43-07:00","id":129342,"title":"","content":"I suppose a lot of this depends on wht sort of game you want to run - do you have any themes or motifs you want to push?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T16:11:15-07:00","id":129353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128239-rural-freeholds?p=129342#post129342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose a lot of this depends on wht sort of game you want to run - do you have any themes or motifs you want to push?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm rather keen on fairy-tales and the Theory of Narrative Causality - you can imagine how thrilled I was to find out about Talecrafting - but I'd also like quite a strong theme of defying the story to be present throughout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T16:54:22-07:00","id":129405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thornfield13713</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128239-rural-freeholds?p=129353#post129353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm rather keen on fairy-tales and the Theory of Narrative Causality - you can imagine how thrilled I was to find out about Talecrafting - but I'd also like quite a strong theme of defying the story to be present throughout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not focus the nucleus of the freehold around one of the Stately Homes or Castles in the area, then? The current Monarch holds their seat and meetings there, and each of the other Monarchs have their own traditional properties, and those mark the outline of the freehold - they tend the edges, so to speak. Focus on the spread an isolation of the Changelings and how that leads to some being a touch... eccentric. When they all get together (either for full 'court' or semi-formal meetings) there's a lot of pomp and circumstance and ritual to it, reinforcing the rote-like aspect of fairy tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T17:17:00-07:00","id":131017,"title":"","content":"Well, for what it's worth, I would think back in history. In my world there are three factors that help make a good location for a freehold or court: access to the Hedge (which tend to be places of great natural beauty), a group of mortals for glamour, and an investment of hollow-type magic by the Changeling. The settlement can continue if at least two out of the three continue to give the place power. A freehold might be somewhere that had a decent mortal population for hundreds of years, but happens to have not been too large in the last fifty or hundred years. It's hard for the group to leave because: Changelings still tend to cross over from the Fae lands here, so someone needs to pick up the pieces or its a prime spot for seasonal magic power (perhaps the rituals of seasonal magics need to be at ley line crossings). Perhaps they guard a sleeping Changeling Queen.<br /> <br /> Maybe the group is purposely on the Fringe-- because they have been cast out from the city-based court, so they formed their own freehold. Maybe they hang out here because they are doing some kind of not-so- acceptable business? Maybe they smuggle goblin fruit, do some kind of mortal money/paperwork forgery, or maybe they make tokens that they sell to goblins? Okay, not the best examples, but any actions that they court might want to be able to deny-- how about they &quot;disappear&quot; city mortals that get too much in the way?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if in an area with less population, the Changelings will harvest glamour through dreams as much as possible? It would solve the problem of provoking the limited local population too much by trying to make those high feelings manifest. That could lead to a campaign with more emphasis on dreams and the connection between the Hedge and Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T12:16:45-07:00","id":132606,"title":"","content":"I would say immediately after reading these posts, I was struck by how well something like a Sleepy Hollow feel would work. Farms, Easters, but hose old stories, areas that give the place a feel of danger. Add the mirror of the World if Darkness and you could easily have a murderer or scene of an od murder staining the Hedge. Goblin fruits and Hobs a plenty, and I really like quynce suggestion of a dumping ground, or sight of exile possibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2968-corbien","name":"Corbien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T16:37:56-07:00","id":132869,"title":"","content":"I'd think about doing something with the Lake District seeing as it so dominates the geography of Cumbria. You could have that be the hot spot for the Fae (lots of tourists going walking and lots of places for them to disappear) with the Freehold covering the villages that surround it and catch the changelings who escape it.<br /> <br /> Also, if you have old mines locally then you could have some of them lead to the Hedge. Personally, I find abandoned mines kinda creepy already but they only get worse when they occasionally lead to the fairy nightmare dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:37:23-07:00","id":136284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thornfield13713</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128239-rural-freeholds?p=129288#post129288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And can we please lay off on the 'superstitious simple country folk' stereotype? Alarmingly enough, the twenty-first century did not magically skip over everyone outside the cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do people take insult to things like this when talking about themes and ideas for a game. We're discussing the World of Darkness here, not the real world. We are all aware the twenty-first century didn't leave everyone in the country in the dark, so-to-speak. Just as every city is not a callous den of sin. Yet, those themes are very powerful and certainly make for good storytelling.<br /> <br /> Personally, were I designing a freehold for this area. I would look into history. What is the local history of your area? Who ruled it? How did they rule it? (and I'm talking well before the twenty-first century here, like back before the Romans made everything theirs, when there were still localized kings and such) How did they interact with the nearby kingdoms?<br /> I would look that stuff up and base my freehold largely around that, possibly (unless they fit thematically) dispensing with the Courts entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:21:09-07:00","id":137321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [We're discussing the World of Darkness here, not the real world. </div> </div> </div>The WoD is still based off of the real world, and in this case it's the real world that their players will know intimately, indeed that seems to be the point. There's a difference between excentuating the negative of a setting and inserting themes that don't belong there and are going to come across as very silly. Isolated rural communities in Britain keeping up old superstitions might have worked if it's set up to the 1940s ( or maybe in the very far periphery), but most of present-day rural Britain just isn't isolated enough for that to work. That's doubly so for Cumbria where the major industry is tourism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T08:44:33-07:00","id":138096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128239-rural-freeholds?p=136284#post136284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people take insult to things like this when talking about themes and ideas for a game. We're discussing the World of Darkness here, not the real world. We are all aware the twenty-first century didn't leave everyone in the country in the dark, so-to-speak. Just as every city is not a callous den of sin. Yet, those themes are very powerful and certainly make for good storytelling.<br /> <br /> Personally, were I designing a freehold for this area. I would look into history. What is the local history of your area? Who ruled it? How did they rule it? (and I'm talking well before the twenty-first century here, like back before the Romans made everything theirs, when there were still localized kings and such) How did they interact with the nearby kingdoms?<br /> I would look that stuff up and base my freehold largely around that, possibly (unless they fit thematically) dispensing with the Courts entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I suppose the reason I get so offended by this sort of thing is that I have to put up with it so much from tourists and relatives from the cities. Seriously, you would not believe the sort of nonsense people are prepared to believe about the country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:22:56-07:00","id":138396,"title":"","content":"Cumbria has it's fair share of interesting history. The old kings of Rheged, said to be in Cumbria, traced their line to Old King Cole of legend. So you have old Briton legends to fall back on there. After them, it was split between Northumbria and Strathclyde. Strathclyde, as the &quot;old North&quot;, is the more interesting option faerie-wise, in my opinion. Don't know where your specific area fell, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:44:14-07:00","id":146410,"title":"","content":"I live in a rural area, without the wealth of history that the UK has to draw on, so my advice will be a little different. Being that it was so rural, and the population density so low, the freehold encompassed something like 5 small towns. Most Lost were on a first name basis, but were not closely tied with one another. There was one big gathering every three months, with a small ceremonial gathering every month. The big gatherings took place on solstices/equinoxes, and celebrated the Court in power at the time. These were the only times changelings from other cities really interacted, and it lead to some powerful tensions between the towns and inside courts.<br /> <br /> If you amp up the isolation and play on some of your region's history, those tensions could be even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:02:19-07:00","id":147517,"title":"","content":"I ran a short game set in a very small town in rural Oklahoma because I loved the idea of a tiny, sort of isolated wilderness freehold. Here's some stuff I did that you might pick apart:<br /> <br /> I don't know about small hamlets in Cumbria compared to the American midwest, but I had as a source of tension that the mortal town was slowly dying because practically all the young people had left for places with an actual future and about the only businesses around were antique stores and low-yield family farms. This was mirrored in the freehold itself, which was coming apart at the seams as people began to just give up on the place. The actual Seasonal Court system was worryingly small, maybe a half-dozen people in each one. Autumn's tyrant queen had reigned straight on through Winter before being deposed when all that court could field was a teenage boy, and with Spring's term coming to a close, the bickering old men housed in a Knights of Columbus building that served as the Summer court had failed to decide on a successor. The Spring monarch was a jovial, grandstanding type who seemed to be from another, more hopeful for rural towns era about a hundred years ago, but was proving not to be up to the task of breathing life back into the freehold. Two other camps were growing fast: the Margravate of the Brim had taken up patrolling the tall-grass trods from their pirate fortress when Summer was too busy bickering to step up, but remained uninvolved in local politics beyond a pledge that they would not let the freehold cease to exist, and a mostly antagonistic group called the Wilders who weren't <i>quite</i> privateers, but had taken to living exclusively in the Hedge, encouraging others to let the freehold burn and join them in unmoored liberty, and rapidly losing Clarity without a mortal touchstone of some kind. The upcoming succession with no clear outcome was the situation when a heretofore-unknown Gentry-like being emerged from the Hedge and blew through town, and the meager supply of Autumn sages and Summer warriors had to face (or ferociously deny) the unpleasant truth that their tiny frayed freehold just didn't have the resources or cohesion to stop this threat from overrunning them. So the game had a really fun dynamic where this lurking threat was in the background more as an excuse to explore the freehold's situation and try to rally everyone to join together again than some combat monster to be fought.<br /> <br /> One element I made use of a lot was drifters and vagabonds, outsider characters temporarily passing through who stand out more than they would in a dense urban area. Also in terms of relations with mortals, I felt like I was more able to have mortal NPCs quietly acknowledge the existence of fairies/magic than a skeptical urban professional might. One NPC was &quot;Grandfather Crow&quot;, a very old Cherokee Beast who played up his image as the &quot;wise old mysterious Indian&quot; stereotype and conspicuously abstained from court politics to distract from the true power of his magic and his active plans for the freehold- in a game set in rural Cumbria I might make a character like that as a whimsical-seeming aged advocate for local languages with a keen interest in Celtic religion and ritual. Anyway, there was a good scene when the PCs were trying to find him and dropped some hints to local farmers when there weren't any tourists around, and got a frank &quot;yeah, you mean the guy who makes it rain when the drought's too long. he likes a circle of corn kernels at sundown.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}